{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0162","billNumberShort":"H.B. 162","billNumberLong":"HB0162","fileNumber":"2026FL0980","shortTitle":"Local Sales Tax Modifications","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"WATKICF","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Watkins, Christine F.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies local sales and use tax provisions.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>allows certain municipalities to impose a local option sales and use tax for purposes of funding infrastructure improvements for the municipality's local law enforcement agency;<hr><ltbullet>requires a municipality's legislative body to hold a public hearing before approving the tax;<hr><ltbullet>requires a municipality to deposit tax revenue into a special revenue fund that is separate from the municipality's general fund;<hr><ltbullet>provides for the reauthorization of a tax at the end of the levy period;<hr><ltbullet>addresses the administration and collection of the tax;<hr><ltbullet>allows the State Tax Commission to retain an administrative charge from collected tax revenue; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Gus Harb","fiscalAnalyst":"Andrea Wilko","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"TOEJRTRYVF","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-07 09:49:03.013","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-07 09:49:03.013","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote